      <h2 style="font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);line-height:.95;color:#1A1A1A;letter-spacing:-.01em">ROOF MAINTENANCE FAQS</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">How often should I have my roof maintained in Florida?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Twice a year, once in Spring before hurricane season and once after it ends, is the baseline for Tampa Bay. That said, if your roof is over 15 years old or you've had recurring issues, adding a mid-summer check is usually worth it. Florida's heat and UV exposure wear down roofs faster than most climates, and this two-visit schedule lets us catch problems at the season boundaries when they're most likely to develop.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">What does roof maintenance include?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Our maintenance service includes a full roof inspection, debris removal, gutter cleaning, flashing and sealant reapplication where needed, minor repair of cracked or loose materials, ventilation check, and a condition report with photos. We address small problems on the spot so they don't grow into major issues.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">Can maintenance really extend my roof's lifespan?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Industry data consistently shows that regular professional maintenance can add 5-10 years to a roof's lifespan. By addressing minor wear, keeping drainage clear, and maintaining sealants and flashing, you prevent the cascading damage that leads to premature replacement. The cost of annual maintenance is a fraction of what a new roof costs.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">Do you offer a maintenance plan or program?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes. Happy Roof offers seasonal maintenance programs that include scheduled inspections and maintenance visits throughout the year. Contact us at (813) 595-7663 to learn about our current maintenance program options and pricing for your property.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">Will roof maintenance affect my insurance?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Generally in a positive direction. Florida insurers tend to look more favorably on well-maintained roofs, and having a documented maintenance history can help support any insurance claim since you're able to demonstrate that the property has been responsibly cared for. Some carriers also require documented maintenance to keep certain coverage provisions valid, particularly for older roofs.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">What happens if you find damage during a maintenance visit?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Minor issues (loose shingles, cracked sealant, small debris damage, and the like) will be handled during your scheduled maintenance visit at no extra charge. For anything more time-intensive, we'll document it with photos and give you a written estimate to help you decide what to do moving forward.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">What roof maintenance can I safely do myself?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">You can usually clean the gutters in spring and fall, trim branches back, and check the attic twice a year for stains or moisture on your own. Things like walking on the roof, pressure washing, patching active leaks, and any work around flashing, skylights, chimneys, or vents, however, are best left to professionals.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',this.getAttribute('aria-expanded')==='true'?'false':'true');this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('open')">How can I prevent roofing algae and moss growth?<svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1A1A1A" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">The dark streaks you see on your roof might be <em>Gloeocapsa magma</em>, a type of algae that thrives in heat and humidity. Left alone, it can hold moisture against your shingles and shorten their lifespan. If prevention is your goal, we'll install zinc ridge strips on any existing roof and include algae-resistant shingle options in every replacement quote. If you already have streaks and want them removed, the only appropriate method is a professional low-pressure soft wash.</div></div>
